There are no notes.

## Suggestions (not running)

A suggestion is a tool that pipegen does not run for you. It may be a tool pipegen has not reviewed, or a reviewed tool that had nothing to run on in this repository (its reason says which). Suggestions are mention-only: they never run. A tool can join the reviewed list only through a reviewed pull request to pipegen.

There are no suggestions.

## Files pipegen created and why

- \`PIPEGEN.md\`: this file.
- \`.github/workflows/pipegen.yml\`: the workflow that starts the pipeline. Its jobs sit beside it in \`.github/workflows/pipegen-merge.yml\`, \`.github/workflows/pipegen-push.yml\` and \`.github/workflows/pipegen-nightly.yml\`.
- Dependabot, in \`.github/dependabot.yml\` when pipegen adds an entry: it keeps the pinned actions up to date, each update at least 7 days old. The entry ignores the central repository, because Dependabot can not read it, so Dependabot does not bump the central commit. pipegen keeps that pin fresh: \`npx pipegen update\` opens the pull request and the nightly run warns when the pin is old. There are two opt-ins, not on by default: an organisation grant through the API, or a git registry entry with a read-only token you make yourself. A repository that uses Renovate keeps it and gets no Dependabot file (set \`minimumReleaseAge\` to 7 days in Renovate).
- Files that were already in your repository, identical to what pipegen writes, are listed in the setup pull request. pipegen never rewrites them, and uninstall asks before it deletes one.

## Your tests

Starter tests describe what your code does today. They are a coverage floor, not proof: they can lock in today's bugs, so review them. App code runs with full power (process, network and files), so the CI job that runs it has no secrets, a read-only token and no network except the registry.

No test decision was recorded.

